# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a loop with a backward OP_JMP hits a safepoint on each iteration;
#         the safepoint decrements instruction_budget_remaining and checks
#         the step budget, preventing infinite-loop starvation.
#
# defer-to: T39
#
# Reason: verifying that safepoint fires on every backward branch iteration
# requires either (a) a tunables header to set a tiny budget so the yield
# is observable, or (b) a host-driver assertion on instruction_budget_remaining
# mid-loop.  Neither is available in the REPL-only chk runner at M3.
# A pure-urbiscript version (counting loop) would run to completion without
# any observable yield signal.  T39 introduces the ## host: mechanism.
#
# While a tight urbiscript loop (e.g. "var i = 0; while (i < 3) i = i + 1; i")
# does exercise the backward-branch safepoint path, verifying the *safepoint*
# specifically (not just correctness of the loop result) requires T39 hooks.
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by:
#   ## tunables: URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX=2
#   var i = 0; while (i < 5) { i = i + 1 }; i
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 5
